# Notes — one sentence per line

When you write mentor notes (`notes/`, `week-NN.md` deltas, anything that lands in the notes repo), **each sentence that ends with `.` goes on its own line.**

Do not pack two sentences into one paragraph.

## Bad

> Front walks `n`. Then both until front has no next. Back sits before the victim.

## Good

> Front walks `n`.
>
> Then both until front has no next.
>
> Back sits before the victim.

Headings, lists, and code fences stay as they are.

A line that is not a sentence (a heading, a table row, a URL) does not get a fake period.

This is **notes only**. Chat still follows `.cursor/rules/lc-voice.mdc`.
